#{[17592186495004 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495004 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495004 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495004 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495004 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495004 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495004 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495004 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495004 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b6be27ac-a148-5263-8d74-f364a5f6e009" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495039 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495039 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495039 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495039 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495039 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f9a522c8-2da3-5f8b-a8d6-4f543f912c76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495057 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495057 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44808" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495057 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495057 #edb/ref 1071 "A bouquet of flowers consists of $5$ roses and $4$ violets. The cost of one rose is $R$ dollars and the cost of one violet is $V$ dollars. Joseph is purchasing some bouquets for a graduation ceremony, and his total bill comes to $10(5R+4V)$ dollars.\n\nWhat does the factor $10$ mean in this context?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495057 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0fdb87d2-4260-5682-92a9-c298d9309d20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495057 #edb/ref 1074 "Five roses cost $5R$ dollars and four violets cost $4V$ dollars. Thus, the cost, in dollars, of a bouquet is\n\n$$\n5R+4V.\n$$\n\nJoseph's bill, in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n10(5R+4V).\n$$\n\nThis is $10$ times the cost of a single bouquet. Thus, the factor $10$ must be the total number of bouquets that Joseph purchased." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495070 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495070 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110315" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495070 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495070 #edb/ref 1071 "In a cinema, a snack combo consists of four hot dogs, two medium fries, and two medium soft drinks. The cost of one hot dog is $H$ dollars, the cost of one portion of fries is $F$ dollars and the cost of one drink is $D$ dollars. Alan is purchasing some combos for his friends and the total bill comes to $5(4H+2F+2D)$ dollars. \n\nWhat does the factor $5$ mean in this context?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495070 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "261e2c7f-a2b0-5f74-8412-23a24f65f2b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495070 #edb/ref 1074 "A hot dog costs $H$ dollars, one medium fries costs $F$ dollars, and a medium soft drink costs $D$ dollars. Thus, the cost, in dollars, of a combo is\n\n$$\n4H+2F+2D.\n$$\n\nAlan's bill, in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n5(4H+2F+2D).\n$$\n\nHence, the factor $5$ must be the total number of combos that he's purchased." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495077 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495077 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110213" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495077 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495077 #edb/ref 1071 "The fee a plumber charges for a callout is given by the expression $45h+50,$ where $h$ is the time, in hours, it takes him to complete the job. \n\nWhat does the constant term of the expression represent in this context?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495077 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c3cdc1a-ff2a-59c0-9009-f0a0d149abd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495077 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression tells us that the plumber charges $$45$ every hour, plus a 'base fee' of $$50.$ \n\nThe constant term is $50.$ This represents the fee (in dollars) the plumber charges for working zero hours." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495088 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495088 #edb/ref 1069 "q-45109" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495088 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495088 #edb/ref 1071 "A small pizza costs $S$ dollars and a medium drink costs $M$ dollars. Kate is purchasing some pizzas and drinks for her family and the total bill comes to $6S+3M$ dollars. \n\nWhat does the factor $3$ mean in this context?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495088 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5846d998-51e9-574a-9a51-5526adf86d55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495088 #edb/ref 1074 "A small pizza costs $S$ dollars and a medium drink costs $M$ dollars.\n\nKate's bill, in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n6S+3M.\n$$\n\nHence, the factor $3$ must be the total number of medium drinks that Kate purchased." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495112 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495112 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75774" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495112 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495112 #edb/ref 1071 "Sophie reserves a hotel room. The price of the room is $T$ dollars and, additionally, she must pay a $9%$ luxury tax.\n\nWhich expression gives the total cost, in dollars, of the hotel room after tax is applied?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495112 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9076f1fb-4181-58aa-adca-483a1b65f8fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495112 #edb/ref 1074 "The price before taxes of a hotel room is $T$ dollars.\n\nThe amount of taxes Sophie pays is  $9%$ of the price of the hotel room, or $0.09T.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of the  hotel room after luxury tax is:\n\n \n\n$$\nT+0.09T\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495117 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495117 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110161" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495117 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495117 #edb/ref 1071 "For babysitting, Mia receives payment, in dollars, given by the expression $35h+15,$ where $h$ is the time, in hours, she spends babysitting. \n\nWhat does the coefficient of $h$ represent in this context?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495117 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9962cae8-99a7-590f-a35c-df110645462c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495117 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression tells us that Mia is paid $$35$ for each hour, plus a 'base fee' of $$15.$\n\nThe coefficient of  $h$ is $35.$  This represents the fee Mia charges for each hour she spends babysitting." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495120 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495120 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44815" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495120 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495120 #edb/ref 1071 "Paul is buying a cell phone at an online store. The price of the cell phone is $P$ dollars, and Paul also has to pay $$15$ for the shipping and handling of the product.\n\nWhat expression represents the total cost, in dollars, of the cell phone?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495120 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a52234c2-10d3-5f1e-bf78-705f84575746" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495120 #edb/ref 1074 "The price of the cell phone is $P$ dollars.  \n\nThe amount for shipping and handling is $$15.$\n\n Hence, Paul's total bill for the cell phone will be $P+15$ dollars." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495140 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495140 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110281" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495140 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495140 #edb/ref 1071 "Mike is going to buy a baseball bat. The price of the bat is $P$ dollars, and Mike also has to pay a tax of $12%.$\n\nWhich expression represents the total cost of the bat, in dollars, after applying the tax?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495140 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c61855c0-f32e-503f-84bf-b1654b65b8ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495140 #edb/ref 1074 "The price of the bat before taxes is $P$ dollars. \n\nThe amount of tax Mike has to  pay is $12%$ of the price of the bat, or $0.12P.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of the bat after tax is:\n\n \n\n$$\nP+0.12P\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495141 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495141 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110306" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495141 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495141 #edb/ref 1071 "The retail price of a particular model of cell phone, at Jordan's Electronics, is \n$C$ dollars and the purchaser also has to pay an $11%$  tax.\n\nWhich expression represents the total cost, in dollars, of the cell phone after tax is applied?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495141 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c71a7e7c-58e1-5206-bb4a-519f537223c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495141 #edb/ref 1074 "The price of the cell phone before taxes is $C$ dollars.\n\nThe amount of tax the purchaser has to pay is $11%$ of the price of a phone or $0.11C$ dollars.\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of the cell phone after tax is:\n\n \n\n$$\nC+0.11C.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495169 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495169 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110316" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495169 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495169 #edb/ref 1071 "A bouquet of flowers consists of $8$ tulips and $4$ violets. The cost of one tulip is $T$ dollars and  the cost of one violet is $V$ dollars. Thomas is purchasing some bouquets for a wedding, and his total bill comes to $12(8T+4V)$ dollars.\n\nWhat does the factor $12$ mean in this context?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495169 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7d200e6-96cf-5acb-92f7-781b4bd31a5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495169 #edb/ref 1074 "Eight tulips cost $8T$ dollars, and four violets cost $4V$ dollars. Thus, the cost,  in dollars, of a bouquet is\n\n$$\n8T+4V.\n$$\n\nThomas' bill,  in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n12(8T+4V).\n$$\n\nThis is $12$ times the cost of a single bouquet. Thus, the factor $12$ must be the total number of bouquets that Thomas purchased." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495172 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186494920 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495172 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110314" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495172 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495172 #edb/ref 1071 "Mel is buying a skateboard. The price of a skateboard is $P$ dollars, and Mel also has to pay a $18%$ tax.\n\nWhat expression represents the total cost, in dollars, of a skateboard after tax is applied?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495172 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fb9924ff-c4e2-52dd-bf49-e683873b21a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495172 #edb/ref 1074 "The price before taxes of a skateboard is $P$ dollars.\n\nThe amount of tax Mel pays is  $18%$ of the price of a skateboard, or $0.18P.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of the skateboard after tax is:\n\n \n\n$$\nP+0.18P\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
